WEBVTT

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.420
Do you think it's true, sir?

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.110
That if we kill the head witch, 
we'll be given land from the village?

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.740
What is it?

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.770
A... A rat?

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.250
Wh-What's going on?

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.500
Rats!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.440
They're huge!

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.990
We're changing our route!

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.410
Right! Circle to the right!

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.090
Are the troops in the rear still with us?

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.070
What?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.260
My hands!

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.530
My legs!

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.600
What even happened?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.620
What's going on?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.640
This is absurd...

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.100
Commander! Look!

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.340
<b><i>Boo! Did we startle you?</i></b>

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.030
Wh-What?!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.360
What happened?

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.740
What on earth was that?

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.560
Was that magic?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.040
This is what witches can do?

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.320
We're being toyed with?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.770
Retreat.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:53.050
Sir?

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.720
We're lucky to have our lives.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.780
The witches just showed us mercy.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.030
Now, then, this is the current situation.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:23.280
In part because of the students' traps, 
the 10,000 foot soldiers have been routed.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.660
All right!

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.670
One company, however, has skillfully 
avoided the traps and continues its advance,

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.460
nevertheless.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.420
The beastfallen mercenary group, eh?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.800
What's more, in all likelihood, 
a demon-possessed is among them.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.310
Are demon-possessed strong?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.560
They are beastfallen that can use certain 
magic infinitely and without incantation.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.310
Good grief.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:56.570
That is generally not a foe one 
should fight in small numbers.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.820
If you're scared, ya coulda 
evacuated with the villagers.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.870
I reflexively stayed out 
of concern for my frien—

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.170
Lilly!

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.210
You fool!

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.130
Professor Zero!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.690
The start of the battle has been signaled.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.080
Steel your resolve!

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.220
Boss! I caught her alive.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.970
Episode 12   The Beginning of the Adventure

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.520
Now what?

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:29.020
We take her to the village 
and eat her in front of them.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.770
It will be more entertaining 
that killing her here.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.780
I like it!

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.320
Did ya hear that, mouse?

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.530
I can't wait—

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.220
What was that?

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.110
Where'd it come from?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.210
How?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.700
Killing you or keeping you alive...

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.380
Which will make them fight harder?

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.090
K-Killing me!

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.130
Okay. In that case...

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.800
Father!

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.190
Never say that again!

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.650
Never say you should be killed!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.570
It's not regenerating.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.700
My weapon carries a witch curse 
and Church consecration.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.080
It should prove effective 
against a demon-possessed.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.830
Hmm... That hurts.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.120
Father, his arm is back!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.850
I can tell that much even without seeing it.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.230
Stay quiet, or you'll die.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.840
Oops.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.990
My bad. I got some on you.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.600
So this guy's the demon-possessed?

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.160
This is getting slightly interesting.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.710
They're all coming back to life!

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.890
Lilly, hide in the treetops.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.430
Y-Yes, Father!

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.460
It's true that I am not strong,

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.650
but I cannot stand being taken lightly.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.620
Uh-oh, now he's mad.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.530
I'll take the demon-possessed. 
I'll let you have the rest.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.200
Let's get started.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.540
What?!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.280
You fell right into it!

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.650
It was basically a kid's trap.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.400
Tyrant, you bastard! You betrayed us?!

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.650
They're using magic!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.130
Kill those three!

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.380
Spread out!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.920
There are only four of 'em! We can 
overwhelm them with our numbers!

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.810
Are you certain about that?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.300
At a rough glance,

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.450
I'd say the horned girl made 30, 
the lizard made 10,

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.680
and the young man made five.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.250
What matters most is not how many 
you create, but how many hit.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.400
Wh-What was that?!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:07.940
Run!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.620
Aim carefully, students.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.990
Zahard Rohud!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.730
Run my quarry through!

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.130
Chapter of Hunting, verse two!

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.160
Steim!

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.250
Grant me power!

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:31.690
We're not hitting as many 
as I thought we would.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.430
Because they took shelter, 
using trees and boulders as shields.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.430
Your opponents are experienced warriors. 
What is your next move?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.520
Damn it! Those brats!

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.960
Kill 'em!

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.690
Take this!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.450
Hey! One's headed your way!

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.700
Ha-hah!

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.300
Sayb!

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.960
Don't worry. I've got this.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.920
Wow, Sayb! A new move!

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.970
D-Don't accidentally touch me, dude!

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.980
Then I'll bring out my trump card!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:28.830
Ta-dah!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.450
A no-incantation Flagis 
with ultra-precise targeting!

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.090
Oh, snap...

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.120
I-I overdid it, a little.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.910
I swear...

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.130
I've got it.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.260
Now,

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.790
tell me, beastfallen soldiers.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.260
What is your next move?

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.900
What was that all of a sudden?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.420
You okay, old man?

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:32.420
Who're ya callin' old man? 
I'll wring your neck!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.140
You piece of shit!

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:48.010
It's no use. I can't kill him dead.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.520
Damn.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.690
Sorry, Witch! Give me a little help!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.600
I shall handle it.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.950
I am in top form now, after all.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.340
Students, I shall set a bad example for you.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.830
Mercenary, on my signal,

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.320
retreat outside the wall.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.590
H-Hey! I didn't ask you to go that far!

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:18.120
Ard Gehrd In De Cor Dia Zea.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:24.520
In the name of the King of Despair who leered
from the crossroads of desire and longing,

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:29.210
come forth from the mud-black
abyss, O Gate of Decay!

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.230
Servants of strife bound
by contract of blood and flesh,

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:37.080
Descend on this fool's wild banquet and feast!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.490
Get back, Mercenary!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.700
You got it!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.880
Forbidden Chapter, final page!

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.910
Segtor Medis!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.970
Grant me power, for I am Zero!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.000
Arisen dead,

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.750
it's mealtime!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.900
Is this magic, too?

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.990
If an outstanding mage 
goes down the wrong path,

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.220
they could easily bring the world to ruin.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.030
So...

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.120
Don't go astray.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.850
It would take a bit of work to vanquish you.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.970
My, how delightful!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:25.830
If it's a show like this, I would 
welcome one every year!

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:31.170
This is pretty expensive, 
so I'd rather it not be every year.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:35.720
You have the VIPs of the Seven Great 
Cathedrals here to observe these exercises?

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.510
Yep. All of them.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:38.480
And the culprit?

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.960
We've identified him.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.240
All that's left is to create 
irrefutable circumstantial evidence

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.360
in front of the largest audience possible.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.860
If it wouldn't be a problem, 
might I hazard a guess?

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:50.700
Hey! You're too close to her!

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:54.710
Bingo. You've—

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.460
Something's coming.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.260
Remnants of Disaster!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.230
Those vermin eat people!

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.220
Protect the Bishops!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.890
Mage Commander Amnir!

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.770
Mages!

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.400
Prepare to cast Firam!

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.640
Reduce the foes before us to ash!

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:22.790
Princess,

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:27.660
I believe you have already 
noticed, but isn't that...

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:33.580
Bag Do Wal Fel Do Al!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.540
O great serpent that slumbers in inferno!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.420
Awaken from the cradle of
assembled hellfire and incinerate!

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.850
Chapter of Harvest, page seven!

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.140
Firam!

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.620
Grant me power!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:54.890
What?

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.590
Yeah. As I thought.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:03.610
Raul!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.170
Gather near me, all of you!

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:28.940
If you come near me, you'll be safe. Come!

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.430
Bishop Ideamor, 
Your Excellency, what is this?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.500
Chief Mage Albus...

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.950
It appears the witch 
of the village you trusted

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:41.850
is willing to produce great casualties 
to protect her village.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.910
I harbored suspicions from the beginning.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.190
Therefore I prepared a countermeasure.

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.970
A countermeasure?

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:53.700
You know of a way to repel 
these foul creatures?

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.950
Why did you not speak up earlier?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.240
I wanted to believe...

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.750
In the goodness of the village witch,

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:07.960
as well as the ability 
of Wenias's Chief Mage.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.400
Unfortunately, this is the reality.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:13.070
Now do come to my side, Mr. Torres.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:18.300
The ward's effects do not extend 
beyond my reach, at best.

00:15:18.860 --> 00:15:20.560
You know,

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.800
you can't create a ward without 
knowing the name of the foe's demon.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.780
Bishop Ideamor, Your Excellency,

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.780
how do you possess knowledge of which demon

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.270
is the source of that Remnant of Disaster?

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.390
Please do explain.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.210
Because a noble's private 
soldiers discovered it

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:44.500
and "certain Church extremists" 
had secreted it away,

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.760
none of the other bishops 
had seen it before.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.810
So how did Your Excellency prepare a ward

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.220
against that Remnant 
of Disaster ahead of time?

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.460
Bishop Ideamor...

00:15:58.010 --> 00:16:00.360
No... I...

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:07.520
They're here! The R-Remnant of Disaster!

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.340
How can this be?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.910
I am in possession of a ward!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:19.550
Why isn't it working? My ward!

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:22.020
My ward!

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:34.680
Boo!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:37.690
Did I startle thee?

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.220
A powerful performance!

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:49.620
I nearly believed a swarm of Remnants 
of Disaster had actually rushed in!

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:57.320
Once the curtain rises, 
even if the start time is far off,

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.870
performers will naturally appear.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.210
Thy performance was quite fine,

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:04.330
comical as it was.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.080
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:11.960
I am fond of humans' flexibility 
to correct the error of their ways.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.840
I shan't kill thee.

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.820
Shouldst thou demonstrate obedience,

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.340
thou mayest keep thy 
position as bishop as well.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:25.100
As I thought, you rigged your peasant 
soldiers with Remnants of Disaster, too...

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.520
knowing that if those 
who fled turned into monsters,

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.110
thou couldst blame it on the witches.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:37.240
Thy influence shall prove useful 
in stopping the south's witch hunts.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.400
However...

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.370
Th-That's...

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:48.060
My dear Ludens left this thing 
that was in Kady's stomach uneaten.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:49.360
Kady?

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:52.540
Eat it.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:53.250
What?!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:54.040
Go on.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:55.380
I-I can't!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.720
Why not?

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:01.010
Didst thou not feed this 
to people seeking salvation?

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:04.620
Telling them it was a "divine blessing"?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.990
Eat it. That is necessary to forgiving thee.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.430
P-P-Please, sp-spare—

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:13.550
Here!

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:15.500
Swallow it.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.940
One nice gulp.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.540
Very well! Forgiven!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:35.250
They gathered 10,000 people 
and couldn't subdue one village?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.650
Pathetic!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.390
The witches didn't inflict a single casualty.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.010
How compassionate of them!

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:45.560
I heard those scoundrels brought 
a Remnant of Disaster down from the north.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:52.680
<i>The large-scale military action 
the anti-witch faction took</i>

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:57.410
<i>ended as an amusing farce to be 
passed down through generations.</i>

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.960
Well, everything worked out!

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:05.910
What's the saying: 
"After rain comes fair weather"?

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.830
All three of you truly performed admirably!

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:14.340
Now, as for the reason 
I summoned you three here...

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.680
Ta-dah! Your diplomas!

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:19.630
Whoo!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:24.840
Congratulations!

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:26.840
Huh?

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:28.430
Why don't you look happy?

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:31.350
We thought we might be getting tested again.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:34.090
And that we'd fail if we were 
too happy about it.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:34.940
Yup.

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:38.260
Oh, Holdem!

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:42.450
The students have lost 
their capacity to trust!

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.950
You're the reason they lost it, my lady.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.360
Hey, Headmaster.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:51.960
Now that we've graduated, 
you'll help find us a job, right?

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:54.960
Oh? You're interested?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.360
I am!

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.110
I wanna enlist with 
the Church & Mage Knights.

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:02.970
I think I'd like to research 
magic a little more.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:07.780
What if I told you I had 
the perfect jobs for you?

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:17.820
And so the three of us returned 
to field program village to gather our things.

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.320
Go ahead. Take it.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.020
The book is yours.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:29.560
But... to you, this is a memento 
of your brother, isn't it?

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.180
It's also a memento of your father.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.670
Besides, I never managed to decipher it.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:40.760
Um, at the end it says, "To my brethren."

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.010
That means you, right, Professor Zero?

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:48.050
My brother was always a little bothersome.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.120
Not that. The numbers.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.960
Look at the numbers for the allotments 
for the potions in the book.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.060
Turn "13" to "0."

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.730
If you do...

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.300
The allotments on every page change, see?

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.970
Ridiculous! It was that simple?

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:09.350
It's simple, but it's funny.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:14.070
It's a code that's impossible to break 
if you don't know Thirteen wrote the book.

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:18.500
I'm glad you're the one who had 
this book, Professor Zero.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.930
Goodbye for now, my dear nephew.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:34.290
Aunt Zero... should I call you that?

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:42.380
Take care, you three.

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:49.170
You're <i>really</i> gonna leave 
the Tyrant in this village?

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:50.700
Isn't that dangerous?

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:54.220
It's not dangerous! Just trust me already!

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:56.710
Never gonna happen.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.330
Here. Eat this on the road.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.210
Lilly, I'll miss you!

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:07.720
What are you, Kudo's mom?

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.720
I'm not one for long goodbyes.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:12.380
Be on your way.

00:22:13.400 --> 00:22:14.430
Laios.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:18.480
You said you'd go on a journey with me!

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:20.480
I'll come back to get you,

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:24.080
if you haven't forgotten me 
once you've grown up.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:29.140
I'm already halfway to being 
a grown-up, you know!

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:30.250
You're right.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:34.960
The time went by so fast.

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:37.840
Yeah, even though so much happened.

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:42.750
Still, do you think our 
next job will go okay?

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:45.510
The Forbidden Library?

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:46.710
Yes.

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:50.760
You'll gather and bring back information 
about Remnants of Disaster.

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:54.150
To be honest, the mission 
is deadly dangerous.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:01.590
I'm incredibly happy I get to be 
with the two of you after graduation.

00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:03.770
I love you both.

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:08.280
How can you say something 
so embarrassing, dude?

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:11.370
Why are you making me like you even more,

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:13.900
when you're not gonna have feelings for me?

00:23:13.900 --> 00:23:15.030
Just why?

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:17.600
That's right! That's cruel, dude!

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:19.690
That wasn't my inten—

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:21.540
Oh, sorry, my motion sickness is here.

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.040
Already?!

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:24.820
O-Open the window!

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:27.480
Barf outside, Sayb! Outside!

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.420
Hey! Don't be so rowdy in the carriage!

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:29.930
It makes flying difficult!

00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:36.300
I'd love to see Professor Los.
